--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8de559a088a5d4d48bb00ae8ccc21165, type: 3}
  m_Name: Alien Invasion
  crisisName: Alien Invasion
  resolutionSplash: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ee161ddb999416b4f9c5f8536c8f1f18, type: 3}
  crisisStartSplash: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 3fdcd1a17f6968b46ab0eacaf44bf018, type: 3}
  obviousWarningSplash: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 745f6780a7c997c48941d1a7cc63ac79, type: 3}
  ominousWarningSplash: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5136a3ead82da1d409307b3ccc2defd4, type: 3}
  ominousWarningText: "Unknown objects have entered our skies. Observatories first detect them beyond the atmosphere, moving along trajectories that no natural object and no known spacecraft should be capable of following. Their courses change without visible propulsion, sometimes stopping or turning in ways that defy conventional orbital mechanics. Civilian pilots and military radar stations begin reporting the same contacts, confirming that the phenomenon is neither an instrument failure nor an astronomical mistake. Attempts at radio communication, visual signaling, and encoded transmission receive no identifiable response. More objects appear behind the first. Whatever they are, they are approaching deliberately."
  obviousWarningText: "The objects are artificial. High-resolution observations reveal structured hulls, coordinated formations, and deliberate changes in course as several craft descend toward populated regions, military facilities, and strategic infrastructure. Every available channel of communication has been usedâ€”radio, light, digital transmission, mathematical sequences, and signals designed to demonstrate peaceful intentâ€”without receiving an answer that anyone can recognize. Aircraft scramble while radar installations track vessels whose size and capabilities remain uncertain. Civilians gather beneath the sky as shapes once visible only on screens emerge through clouds large enough to be seen with the naked eye. They are descending now. We still do not know why."
  crisisStartText: "They have arrived. Unknown vessels now occupy our skies, deploying forces whose technology appears to exceed anything our civilization expected to confront at this stage of history. Alien units are descending near strategic regions and may attack cities, infrastructure, or military forces while additional craft remain overhead. Their intentions are not yet fully understood: some civilizations may seek communication, others may meet the invaders in battle, and scientists will inevitably search for opportunities to study technology left behind. Their superiority is formidable, but not absolute. For the first time, our civilization faces an enemy that did not arise from this worldâ€”and whatever happens next will define humanity's place beyond it."
  resolutionText: "The skies are quiet again. The alien vessels that once darkened our horizon have withdrawn, been destroyed, or fallen silent, and for the first time in months watchtowers report nothing overhead but ordinary clouds. Salvage crews comb the wreckage left behind, recovering fragments of technology that may reshape our understanding of what is possible. Survivors speak carefully of what they witnessed, aware that no explanation yet accounts for why the invaders came or why they finally left. Some communities celebrate a victory hard-won; others quietly bury the dead and rebuild what was lost. Whatever answers still wait among the stars, our civilization has proven that it can face an enemy from beyond the world and endure. We are no longer the same people who first looked up in wonder and fear."
  ominousWarningTurns: 1
  obviousWarningTurns: 1
  durationTurns: 18
  useAgeWindow: 1
